An easy-to-pick-up graphics layer for Zig: a small package that lets you write
graphical applications and games without wrestling with SDL directly. Objects,
scenes, screens, drawables and scripts compose into something close to a
minimal game engine.

# Design

- Drawables are shapes with a pluggable draw strategy — Rect and other
geometric shapes ship built-in, plus interactive UI ones (Button, TextInput,
Select, Checkbox) and SVG; you can write your own.
- Scripts attach behavior to objects, with start/update/end hooks. A Movement
script and a rigid-body/collision pair are included, and custom scripts are
just structs.
- Scenes hold objects and behave like cameras (zoom and pan); screens own the
render loop and event manager. SDL3 stays reachable underneath when you need it.

Compatible with Zig ^0.16.0, with examples you can run via
`zig build example:moving-box`.
